WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.188 --> 00:00:04.021
(uplifting music)

00:00:05.307 --> 00:00:06.741
- [Mutua] I think people are affected

00:00:06.741 --> 00:00:08.658
by the images they see.

00:00:09.637 --> 00:00:13.404
Most of the time that you
see images coming from Kenya,

00:00:13.404 --> 00:00:17.626
specifically, in most of Africa,
it will be war, disease,

00:00:17.626 --> 00:00:20.459
AIDS, famine, something like that.

00:00:21.971 --> 00:00:25.058
While that is true,
there's still a lot more

00:00:25.058 --> 00:00:28.209
coming out of the continent
that is uplifting,

00:00:28.209 --> 00:00:31.388
that is positive, that is encouraging.

00:00:31.388 --> 00:00:35.091
My mission is to change
our own perceptions

00:00:35.091 --> 00:00:37.841
of what Africa is supposed to be.

00:00:40.478 --> 00:00:42.092
(uplifting music)

00:00:42.092 --> 00:00:45.460
My name is Mutua Metheka,
and I'm a photographer.

00:00:45.460 --> 00:00:48.176
I got into photography by accident.

00:00:48.176 --> 00:00:51.068
A friend of mine showed
me something on a website,

00:00:51.068 --> 00:00:52.942
and I was like, I probably can do this,

00:00:52.942 --> 00:00:54.543
so I decided to try it out.

00:00:54.543 --> 00:00:56.484
(light uplifting music)

00:00:56.484 --> 00:00:59.199
Originally, my mission was
to, you know, educate the West

00:00:59.199 --> 00:01:01.047
on what Africa is like.

00:01:01.047 --> 00:01:02.543
And I realized, it doesn't matter

00:01:02.543 --> 00:01:05.998
what other people think, if
we still think of ourselves

00:01:05.998 --> 00:01:08.165
as backward or not worthy.

00:01:09.616 --> 00:01:11.915
So, my mission changed
to trying to get people

00:01:11.915 --> 00:01:14.085
who have grown up in
African cities to learn

00:01:14.085 --> 00:01:16.252
to see Africa differently.

00:01:17.249 --> 00:01:20.596
If I can keep shooting
what I want people to see,

00:01:20.596 --> 00:01:23.003
then I believe over time
this changes what people

00:01:23.003 --> 00:01:24.670
think of themselves.

00:01:28.462 --> 00:01:31.045
(upbeat music)

00:01:32.711 --> 00:01:35.562
I have recently just
completed a project where

00:01:35.562 --> 00:01:37.828
rock climbing communication masts

00:01:37.828 --> 00:01:40.604
from all over the country.

00:01:40.604 --> 00:01:43.847
The aim was to explore different views

00:01:43.847 --> 00:01:46.123
from this new perspective.

00:01:46.123 --> 00:01:48.122
(uplifting music)

00:01:48.122 --> 00:01:51.354
I can almost guarantee that
no photographer in Africa

00:01:51.354 --> 00:01:54.283
or in Kenya has photographed
from the heights

00:01:54.283 --> 00:01:56.699
that I photographed from.

00:01:56.699 --> 00:01:58.189
So it was a unique opportunity

00:01:58.189 --> 00:02:00.435
and a very rare chance for me.

00:02:00.435 --> 00:02:03.268
(uplifting music)

00:02:06.292 --> 00:02:08.772
We traveled about seven/eight days,

00:02:08.772 --> 00:02:11.367
climbed seven masts in total,

00:02:11.367 --> 00:02:13.933
some going as high as 100 meters.

00:02:13.933 --> 00:02:17.024
It was hard climbing,
but you get to the top,

00:02:17.024 --> 00:02:18.621
and you see the view that awaits you,

00:02:18.621 --> 00:02:21.786
and it's like another world.

00:02:21.786 --> 00:02:24.619
(uplifting music)

00:02:25.979 --> 00:02:28.646
It was beautiful being up there.

00:02:31.517 --> 00:02:33.179
(uplifting music)

00:02:33.179 --> 00:02:35.089
Photography has a unique way of being able

00:02:35.089 --> 00:02:39.135
to change perceptions just
by seeing something different

00:02:39.135 --> 00:02:40.821
over and over and over.

00:02:40.821 --> 00:02:42.483
(uplifting music)

00:02:42.483 --> 00:02:44.288
All of these things are
connected to the value

00:02:44.288 --> 00:02:48.796
that you place on the
place that you live in.

00:02:48.796 --> 00:02:52.675
I think if we see that
what we have is really

00:02:52.675 --> 00:02:54.424
beautiful and worth protecting,

00:02:54.424 --> 00:02:57.059
then we put a lot more
effort into protecting it

00:02:57.059 --> 00:02:59.266
for ourselves and for the future.

00:02:59.266 --> 00:03:02.099
(uplifting music)

